/**
@file structure.dox
@brief Directory documentation, so the generated site has the shape the source tree has.
*/

/** @dir src/engine/ecs
    @brief The ECS: entities, the open type-erased Scene, and every component.

    Storing a component needs no registration. Saving one needs a reflect block and a row
    in VKM_SCENE_COMPONENTS (io/scene/scene_components.h); replicating one,
    NetSchema::replicate. */

/** @dir src/engine/ecs/component
    @brief The components the engine itself understands: plain data that systems read. */

/** @dir src/engine/core
    @brief The Engine and its frame: the stages, the System contract and FrameContext, the clock,
    the host's chrome and its debug view, the graphics settings, the input map, and opening a
    project. */

/** @dir src/engine/base
    @brief The foundation: what every other folder stands on. It includes nothing in the engine
    above it. */

/** @dir src/engine/base/math
    @brief Vector and matrix helpers on top of glm, and the engine's axis convention. */

/** @dir src/engine/resource
    @brief Assets: owned once by ResourceManager, referenced by Handle, named for serialization. */

/** @dir src/engine/io/asset/generate
    @brief Procedural meshes, textures and materials a game can build at run time.

    In the engine rather than the tools because a project links the engine and not the
    tools. */

/** @dir src/engine/io
    @brief Reading and writing: scenes, prefabs, the project file, cooked assets. */

/** @dir src/engine/core/frame
    @brief What one frame's systems hand each other, below every system: the products FrameContext
    names (Visibility, PoseBuffer, UIDrawData and the rest) and the events the systems post. */

/** @dir src/engine/system
    @brief The per-frame systems, a directory per subject, each registered at one stage.

    The stage order is declared once, as SystemStage in core/system.h; app/engine_app.h
    places each system at its stage. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/render
    @brief The engine's whole view of rendering: RenderBackend, RenderView, EditorRenderHooks. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/physics
    @brief Rigid bodies, collision, joints, ragdolls, character control and queries. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/script
    @brief The gameplay boundary: Behavior, BehaviorContext, and the module that loads a game's code. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/hierarchy
    @brief Parent-child links, and the world transform resolved from them each frame. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/ui
    @brief In-game UI: an ECS-authored tree resolved into one draw list per frame; not the editor's ImGui. */

/** @dir src/engine/base/container
    @brief The containers everything else is built on: SparseSet, SlotAllocator, TypeRegistry. */

/** @dir src/engine/base/event
    @brief The typed event bus, and the per-type bus it is made of. */

/** @dir src/engine/debug
    @brief Diagnostics: world drawing (DebugDraw, DebugPalette) in draw/, and the recoverable-error sink and a fault latch in error/. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/animation
    @brief Clips, skeletal posing and bone sockets. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/audio
    @brief The audio system: the scene's sources and listener, mixed by vkmAudio, and the acoustics' rays cast over the physics. */

/** @dir src/engine/system/visibility
    @brief What the camera can see: frustum, distance and screen-size culling. */

/** @dir src/engine/net
    @brief Networking: transport, wire format, replication and hiding the latency. */

/** @dir src/engine/platform
    @brief The engine's input vocabulary over vkmPlatform's devices: bindings and their names, and the
    tick's command. The window, threads and processes are vkmPlatform's (modules/vkmPlatform). */
